 | Claude Code's proxy | Claude Code on its own subscription asks Anthropic itself, through the proxy its env names. While any Claude account has a proxy of its own (`AccountProxies`), the `env` of Claude Code's `settings.json` names the proxy of the account it is signed in to (#1807): `HTTPS_PROXY` and `HTTP_PROXY` set to that account's own, else the subscription's `Proxy` (`ProxyOfLogin`), and `NO_PROXY` to loopback; none for `direct` or a SOCKS proxy, which Claude Code can't use. It is written on every switch (`switchLogin`, the user's or `SwitchWhenSpent`), when the Claude subscription is saved, and at the gateway's look every `loginSwitchEvery` (a sign-in made in Claude Code itself). Claude Code reads its env at start, so only sessions started after the switch take it. A proxy key the user set (in either case) is theirs: magpie then writes none and takes out none of theirs. What magpie wrote is kept in `claude-proxy-env.json`, and a key is magpie's only while it holds that value. A `settings.json` that doesn't parse is left as it is. Its log lines name the proxy through `netproxy.Redact`, without its user and password (#1886); the env gets it whole. | [`claude_proxy_env.go`](../../internal/provider/claude_proxy_env.go) |
